{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{1-x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167597 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167597 #edb/ref 1061 31204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167597 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1b8caf6f-2428-5c44-beeb-66136b28cd56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167597 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167598 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167598 #edb/ref 1061 31205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167598 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "63b227f6-59b4-5b4a-9487-4abf040ea99b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167598 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167599 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167599 #edb/ref 1061 31206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167599 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "498469fb-171d-514d-a919-a53218e62672" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167599 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167600 #edb/ref 1061 31207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167600 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "719532f0-a4af-5600-ad0a-b29865e84e93" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167600 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167702 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167702 #edb/ref 1061 32695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167702 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "20757712-075c-58c5-8cc7-4422f34ec28e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167702 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186168092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168092 #edb/ref 1064 "The derivatives of the inverse reciprocal hyperbolic functions are shown below:\n$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x) & =-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}, &  & x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x) & =-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}, &  & x\\in (0,1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x) & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}, &  & x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (1,\\infty )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the derivative of the base inverse reciprocal hyperbolic functions, we can differentiate combinations of these functions, by using the properties of differentiation.\n\nFor example, let's find the derivative of\n\n$$\ny = \\arsech{(-x^2)}\n$$\n\nUsing the formulas above together with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(-{x}^{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(-{x}^{2})\\sqrt{1-{(-{x}^{2})}^{2}}}\\cdot {(-{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{4}}}\\cdot (-2x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168092 #edb/ref 1065 5210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168092 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "dc2da505-a8d0-5680-b8a0-ddeb66c32295" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168092 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524380 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{ln}^